# Manual API tests. Open this file in VS Code with the "REST Client" extension
# and click "Send Request" above each request. Cookies are kept between requests.
# Change the port to the https port shown when you run the API.
# Nadee Example, frontdesk1 and the passwords below are fictitious demo values for local testing only.
@baseUrl = https://localhost:7183

### 1. Not logged in yet: expect 401 Unauthorized
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/me

### 2. Wrong password: expect 401 "Invalid username or password."
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "userName": "admin", "password": "wrong" }

### 3. Log in as admin: expect 200 with roles ["Administrator"]
# VS Code asks for the password when you click Send, so it is never saved in this file.
# @prompt adminPassword
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "userName": "admin", "password": "{{adminPassword}}" }

### 4. Who am I? expect 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/me

### 5. List departments: expect 200 with the starter list (Administration first)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/departments

### 6. Add a receptionist with a login, in one step (fictitious person): expect 201
# Non-clinical staff have no departmentId: the API places them in "Administration".
# Logins are always created from the staff record.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/staff/employees
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Nadee",
  "lastName": "Example",
  "jobTitle": "Receptionist",
  "phone": "0771234567",
  "email": "frontdesk1@example.test",
  "hireDate": "2026-01-05",
  "isActive": true,
  "userName": "frontdesk1",
  "password": "Front#2026",
  "roles": ["Receptionist"]
}

### 7. List users: expect 200, frontdesk1 is linked to Nadee Example
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users

### 8. Log out: expect 204
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/logout

### 9. Log in as the receptionist: expect 200 with mustChangePassword true
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "userName": "frontdesk1", "password": "Front#2026" }

### 10. Change the temporary password: expect 204
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/change-password
Content-Type: application/json

{ "currentPassword": "Front#2026", "newPassword": "Front#2027" }

### 11. Receptionist tries to list users: expect 403 Forbidden
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users

### 12. Log out: expect 204, then request 4 returns 401 again
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/logout

### ---------- Reports (PDF 3.10). Log in as admin first (request 3). ----------

### 13. Patient registrations this month: expect 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/reports/patients

### 14. Revenue for November 2026: expect 200; "collected" equals the sum of the payments in November
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/reports/revenue?fromDate=2026-11-01&toDate=2026-11-30

### 15. Attendance and leave for November 2026: expect 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/reports/staff?year=2026&month=11

### 16. End date before start date: expect 400
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/reports/appointments?fromDate=2026-11-30&toDate=2026-11-01

### ---------- Notifications and forgot password (Step 23) ----------

### 17. Forgot password: always expect 204, even for a username that does not exist.
###     For a real, active username, every administrator gets a "Password reset requested" notification.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/forgot-password
Content-Type: application/json

{ "userName": "frontdesk1" }

### 18. My notifications (log in first, request 3): expect 200 with "items" and "unreadCount"
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/notifications

### 19. How many are unread: expect 200 { "count": ... }
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/notifications/unread-count

### 20. Mark all my notifications as read: expect 204
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/notifications/read-all
